PKGBUILD_RESULT(3)

# NAME

pkgbuild_result - seal complete package-build outcomes

# DESCRIPTION

*build_result::succeeded* requires a sealed request, complete payload manifest,
sealed artifact, and execution-evidence identity. It derives an artifact binding
and complete result identity.

*build_result::failed* requires a sealed request, execution-evidence identity,
and failure-evidence identity. Failed results contain no payload, artifact, or
artifact binding. Public construction cannot represent a partial result.

A successful result states the intended payload and exact artifact bytes. It
does not by itself prove that decoding those bytes yields that payload; that
statement belongs to the separate build/image admission boundary.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgbuild*(3), *pkgbuild_request*(3)
